                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "(I speak English as a primary language and understand a little Spanish, so keep that in mind...)\n\nFor a Unity title, this game actually isn't all that bad.  [i]Gobernators (Parodia politica peruana)[/i] claims to be similar to [i]Rockman/Megaman[/i] and [i]Mighty No.9[/i] from its description alone.   I have not played [i]Mighty No.9[/i], but have played [i]Rockman/Megaman[/i].  This title isn't terrible, but it cannot possibly measure up to the magic [i]Rockman/Megaman[/i] had (Speaking of which, I totally wanna play that now).\n\nThe title of this game translates to \"Governors (Parody of Peru Politics)\", though I can only assume that the only parody aspects is that it may use Peru figureheads as characters and be set in Peru...but I know nothing about Peru (aside from the man who ate his shoe there), so I can't verify its validity.  The story itself?  I'm guessing it's about an alien who wanted to see the Incas, but was centuries too late as Peru is now modernized.  The alien wants to see who's in charge, but has no luck.  When the alien returns to his ship, he finds that it's been scavanged, which pisses him off.  In his anger, I'm guessing he creates madness within the country. (Understandably so)\n\nBasically, this game can be defined as a \"Hold Right To Win\" title with shooting along the way.  You will have to face drone minibosses and a single boss in this 4-level game.  The difficulty is fairly easy with a few difficult, but passable moments.\n\nThe graphics of this game are....pretty bad like [i]A grande bagunça espacial - The big space mess[/i], but it's priced for free, unlike...that long title I just mentioned.  Overall, this game passes in my book.  It's free, there are achievements, and it's short.  The only flaws seem to be that the graphics are subpar and that the replayability is low.  You don't really need to understand Spanish to play this game.\n\n7/10  Run-n'-gun at a free price.  Worth checking out.",
